{"test_case_id": 5, "benchmark": "ai2_arc", "question": "Proteins that are synthesized in ribosomal subunits undergo extensive post-translational modification and are packaged and directed to the appropriate destination. Which structural component of a cell is involved in such modification?\nA. endoplasmic reticulum\nB. lysosomes\nC. mitochondria\nD. Golgi apparatus", "answer": "Proteins synthesized in ribosomal subunits undergo extensive post-translational modification. This process involves modifying proteins after they have been translated from mRNA to prepare them for specific functions within the cell. The structural component of a cell involved in such modifications is responsible for packaging, sorting, and directing these modified proteins.\n\nGiven that this process requires specialized organelles with distinct roles in protein processing and transport, we can infer that it involves components beyond basic cellular structures like ribosomes or mitochondria. Considering the role of endoplasmic reticulum (ER) in synthesis and modification of biological membrane stuff at the cellular level, as well as its involvement in packaging proteins for secretion or other destinations within the cell, ER is a likely candidate.\n\nFinal Answer: A", "score": 0.0, "label": "1"}
