{"test_case_id": 2, "benchmark": "ai2_arc", "question": "Which feature does not form as a result of tectonic plates diverging?\nA. trench\nB. rift valley\nC. ocean basin\nD. mid-ocean ridge", "answer": "A trench is the feature that does not form as a result of tectonic plates diverging.\n\nThis conclusion stems from the understanding that trenches are typically formed at subduction zones, where one plate is forced beneath another. This process is distinct from plate divergence, which involves plates moving apart and creating new crust on either side. The formation of trenches requires the interaction between two plates, one being pushed under the other, a scenario not characteristic of plate divergence.\n\nFinal Answer: A", "score": 1.0, "label": "0"}
